a) Sau $t=3$ giây;
b) Khi nó đạt độ cao lớn nhất (làm tròn kết quả đến chữ số thập phân thứ nhất của mét).

(CD12) Cho $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} f(x)dx=5$ và $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} g(x)dx=-4$. Tính:
a) $\int\limits_{1}^{-2} f(x)dx$
b) $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} -4f(x)dx$;
c) $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} \frac{-2g(x)}{3}\ dx$;
d) $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} \left[ f\left( x \right)+g\left( x \right) \right]dx$;
e) $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} \left[ f\left( x \right)-g\left( x \right) \right]dx$
g) $\int\limits_{-2}^{1} \left[ 3f\left( x \right)-5g\left( x \right) \right]dx$

(CTST12) Tính các tích phân sau:
a) $\int\limits_{1}^{2} \frac{1-2x}{x^{2}}dx$;
b) $\int\limits_{1}^{2} \left( \sqrt{x}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}} \right)^{2}\ dx$;
c) $\int\limits_{1}^{4} \frac{x-4}{\sqrt{x}+2}\ dx$.

loi_giai:
a) $\int\limits_{1}^{2} \frac{1-2x}{x^{2}}\ dx=\int\limits_{1}^{2} \left( \frac{1}{x^{2}}-\frac{2}{x} \right)dx=-\left. \frac{1}{x} \right|_{1}^{2}-\left. 2\ln x \right|_{1}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}-2\ln 2$;
b) $\int\limits_{1}^{2} \left( \sqrt{x}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}} \right)^{2}\ dx=\int\limits_{1}^{2} \left( x+2+\frac{1}{x} \right)dx=\left. \left( \frac{x^{2}}{2}+2x+\ln x \right) \right|_{1}^{2}=\frac{7}{2}+\ln 2$;
c) $\int\limits_{1}^{4} \frac{x-4}{\sqrt{x}+2}\ dx=\int\limits_{1}^{4} (\sqrt{x}-2)dx=\int\limits_{1}^{4} \left( x^{\frac{1}{2}}-2 \right)dx=\left. \left( \frac{2}{3}x\sqrt{x}-2x \right) \right|_{1}^{4}=-\frac{4}{3}$.

a) $\int\limits_{1}^{3} e^{x-2}\ dx=\int\limits_{1}^{3} \frac{e^{x}}{e^{2}}\ dx=\left. \frac{e^{x}}{e^{2}} \right|_{1}^{3}=e-\frac{1}{e}$;
b) $\int\limits_{0}^{1} \left( 2^{x}-1 \right)^{2}\ dx=\int\limits_{0}^{1} \left( 4^{x}-2\cdot 2^{x}+1 \right)dx=\left. \left( \frac{4^{x}}{\ln 4}-2\cdot\frac{2^{x}}{\ln 2}+x \right) \right|_{0}^{1}=1-\frac{1}{2\ln 2}$;
c) $\int\limits_{0}^{1} \frac{e^{2x}-1}{e^{x}+1}\ dx=\int\limits_{0}^{1} \left( e^{x}-1 \right)dx=\left. \left( e^{x}-x \right) \right|_{0}^{1}=(e-1)-1=e-2$.

a) $\int\limits_{0}^{\pi} (2\cos x+1)dx=\left. (2\sin x+x) \right|_{0}^{\pi}=\pi$;
b) $\int\limits_{0}^{\pi} (1+\cot x)\sin xdx=\int\limits_{0}^{\pi} (\sin x+\cos x)dx=\left. (-\cos x+\sin x) \right|_{0}^{\pi}=2$;
c) $\int\limits_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{4}} \tan^{2}x\ dx=\int\limits_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{4}} \left( \frac{1}{\cos^{2}x}-1 \right)dx=\left. (\tan x-x) \right|_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{4}}=1-\frac{\pi}{4}$.

